ories page shows Consulting = \\\"4 transactions\\\" / \\\"$11,050\\\" — both count and total updated correctly.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"With window.print instrumented, clicking \\\"Print Report\\\" for year 2024 invoked print exactly once (__printCalls=1); no JS errors were raised and the page remained intact (year still 2024, net taxable income still $11,106.51). Console reported 0 errors.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Transactions table columns: DATE, DESCRIPTION, CATEGORY, REFERENCE, AMOUNT, TAX, ACTIONS. Summary shows total income +$47,592.50 and expenses -$36,485.99, which match the sum of the 18 listed rows exactly.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Aug 2026 underlying data = +$250.00 income and -$123.45 expense. Dashboard: income $250, expenses $123, net profit $127; recent activity lists both new transactions. Reports (August 2026): income $250, expenses $123.45, profit +$126.55, income-by-category Consulting $250. All match.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Chart Y-axis labels lack precision; non-zero amounts are indistinguishable from zero\", \"actual\": \"Dashboard \\\"Income vs Expenses\\\" chart for Aug 2026 renders an income bar (height 207.7px, $250.00) and an expense bar (height 102.6px, $123.45), but all five Y-axis ticks read \\\"$0k\\\". The axis uses a $Xk format with no decimals, so any value below $500 rounds to \\\"$0k\\\" and cannot be distinguished from zero.\", \"evidence\": null}]}"
